A teammate proposes to send the event inside the database transaction:

```ts
await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
  await tx.query("INSERT INTO orders (id, status) VALUES ($1, 'placed')", [order.id]);
  await producer.send({ topic: "orders.v1", messages: [{ key: order.id, value: JSON.stringify(event) }] });
}); // COMMIT happens here
```

Statement: "Because the send runs inside the transaction, the two writes are atomic: if the send fails the order rolls back, and if the COMMIT fails the event is never delivered."
